# Information Access in the Humanities: Perils and Pitfalls.

**Authors:** Walker, Geraldene, Atkinson, Steven D.

## Abstract
Describes a study that investigated subject retrieval in a group of humanities databases. Scatter by subject field and type of search term is discussed, the effectiveness of natural language and of controlled vocabulary are compared, and implications for system designers concerned with end-user searches in the humanities are suggested. (37 references) (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ428917

